# PHASE 12 — SHARED DATABASE

## 12.1 Centralized Data Architecture

Create a shared data layer for Foundry and its registered applications.

Prefer a local-first architecture.

Use the existing database infrastructure if available. Otherwise, evaluate:

- SQLite for the local backend.
- IndexedDB for browser-side persistence and offline caching.
- Existing cloud storage infrastructure where applicable.

Do not introduce unnecessary external database subscriptions.

All applications should access shared information through controlled repositories or service interfaces.

## 12.2 Database Collections

Establish the following logical data collections:

| Collection | Purpose |
|---|---|
| users | User profiles and preferences |
| workspaces | Foundry workspaces |
| courses | Academic courses |
| assignments | Academic assignments |
| tasks | Tasks and milestones |
| notes | Academic and workspace notes |
| documents | Imported files and metadata |
| document_chunks | Extracted document sections |
| document_embeddings | Retrieval embeddings |
| conversations | AI conversations |
| messages | Conversation messages |
| memories | Approved persistent AI memory |
| flashcard_decks | Flashcard collections |
| flashcards | Individual flashcards |
| quiz_questions | Quiz content |
| study_sessions | Study activity |
| study_guides | Study guide content |
| presentations | Presentation projects |
| lesson_plans | Instructional plans |
| choice_boards | Learning choice boards |
| integration_accounts | Connected account metadata |
| synchronization_jobs | Synchronization history |
| execution_logs | System operations |
| permissions | Application and tool permissions |

Implement database migrations, schema versions, validation, and backup support.

## 12.3 Shared Academic Context

Connect academic records using stable identifiers.

Each applicable record should support:

- Workspace ID.
- Course ID.
- Assignment ID.
- User ID.
- Source document ID.
- Creation timestamp.
- Modification timestamp.
- Revision information.

Changing the active course should update the shared context without unexpectedly overwriting existing application data.

## 12.4 Data Operations

Implement controlled operations for:

- Create.
- Read.
- Update.
- Archive.
- Search.
- Import.
- Export.
- Restore.
- Delete with appropriate permissions.

Prevent applications from directly modifying another application's private data outside registered service interfaces.

