# PHASE 14 — DOCUMENT EXTRACTION ENGINE

## 14.1 Format-Aware Extraction

Implement dedicated document extraction adapters.

| Format | Extraction requirement |
|---|---|
| PDF | Text and page references |
| DOCX | Headings, paragraphs and tables |
| PPTX | Slide titles, text and speaker notes where available |
| XLSX | Worksheet names, cells and structured tables |
| CSV | Rows and columns |
| HTML | Relevant visible text and document structure |
| Markdown | Headings, paragraphs and code blocks |
| TXT | Plain text |
| Google Docs | Structured document content |
| Google Slides | Slide elements and speaker notes |
| Google Sheets | Worksheet ranges and cell values |

Do not assume all document formats can be converted using the same plain-text export method.

## 14.2 Document Processing Pipeline

Implement the following sequence:

```text
Import Document
      ↓
Validate File
      ↓
Identify Format
      ↓
Select Extraction Adapter
      ↓
Extract Content
      ↓
Normalize Structure
      ↓
Preserve Source References
      ↓
Generate Document Chunks
      ↓
Store Extracted Data
      ↓
Queue for Indexing
```

## 14.3 Source References

Preserve source locations where available:

- Document name.
- Document ID.
- Page number.
- Slide number.
- Worksheet name.
- Cell range.
- Section heading.
- Paragraph location.
- Document revision.

These references must remain associated with generated flashcards, study guides, AI answers, and presentations.

## 14.4 Processing Controls

Provide:

- Extract document.
- Preview extracted text.
- Reprocess document.
- Cancel processing.
- View extraction errors.
- View supported formats.

Scanned documents requiring OCR should be marked accordingly.

Do not claim successful extraction when a document contains only unprocessed images.

