# PHASE 17 — GOOGLE OAUTH MANAGER

## 17.1 Centralized Google Authentication

Implement one Google Integration Manager shared across Foundry applications.

Do not implement separate Google account connections for each application.

Support Google OAuth 2.0 authorization using an appropriate flow for the application's deployment architecture.

## 17.2 Authentication Requirements

Support:

- Connect Google account.
- Select account.
- Authorize individual services.
- Incremental authorization.
- Refresh expired access tokens.
- Disconnect account.
- Revoke access.
- Inspect authorized scopes.
- Display actual account connection state.

Use OAuth state validation and PKCE where appropriate.

Store sensitive credentials and refresh tokens in secure backend storage.

Do not embed secrets inside HTML, iframe source documents, localStorage, or public frontend bundles.

## 17.3 Permission Scopes

Start with the narrowest permissions required for each operation.

Use selected-file access where possible.

Request additional scopes only when a user enables a feature that requires them.

Explain which services and information are being authorized.

Never request unrestricted Google account access by default.

## 17.4 Settings Integration

Extend the existing APIs & Integrations settings.

```text
